# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-avc/openavc-drivers/main/avcdriver.schema.json
#
# Sennheiser SpeechLine SL Rack Receiver DW (single-channel digital wireless)
#
# Controls the SL Rack Receiver DW over Sennheiser Sound Control (SSC)
# version 1: JSON objects over UDP port 45, one object per datagram.
#
# Protocol reference: "Sennheiser Sound Control Protocol (SSC) - Developer's
# guide for SpeechLine Digital Wireless", TI 1094 v4.3, chapters 4-9 (SL Rack
# Receiver DW firmware 4.1.1); source_url below.
#
# Wire format (§4): every address is a path of JSON keys. A null argument
# reads it ({"rx1":{"mute_state":null}}), any other value writes it, and the
# reply carries the value now in force, so a set's answer is its read-back.
# A refusal is {"osc":{"error":[{"rx1":{"mute_mode":[406]}}]}} (§8.4, §9).
# Values here are numbers where the multi-channel receiver has words: mute
# mode 0-4, sensitivity 0-6, output gain as an index 0-6 (-24 to +12 dB),
# EQ preset 0-4, transmitter type 0-3, display brightness 0-100.
#
# Push, not polling (§5): the receiver notifies a subscribed client of every
# change on the socket the subscription came from. A subscription lasts the
# lifetime the client asks for (10 s by default, §8.11) and at most 1000
# notifications, then ends with error 310 (§5.1); sending the same request
# again renews it. Every subscribable address is subscribed with a lifetime of
# 90 s and the poll renews them all (the Poll Interval stops at 30 s, so every
# lifetime spans three renewals). A 310 subscribes everything again at once.
# The receiver answers every subscription with the current value, so the
# renewal is also a full resync.
#
# One address per message. The document's only replies that repeat a name at
# one level answer a message that asked for several addresses or methods at
# once: a subscription listing several addresses, or an /osc/xid sent beside
# the subscription (§8.11 examples 1 and 3). A JSON reader keeps the last of a
# repeated name, so OpenAVC 0.38.0 would lose the rest of such a reply. This
# driver sends one address in each message, reads and subscriptions alike, so
# nothing in the document repeats; from the release after 0.38.0 a repeated
# name is read under every copy anyway.
#
# The transmitter. /mates/active reports whether a transmitter is linked
# (§8.52). Most transmitter values have that link as a pre-condition, so they
# are subscribed only while a transmitter is linked, and the moment one links
# (then_query, platform 0.38.0; the poll subscribes them on older releases).
# When the link drops, every value only a linked transmitter reports is
# cleared. Sensitivity and auto power off have no link pre-condition: the
# receiver keeps them, so they are always subscribed and settable.
#
# Level meter: /audio/out1/level_db streams while subscribed, so it is opt-in
# (Enable Level Meter, or Meter On / Meter Off at runtime) and throttled here;
# TI 1094 documents no rate parameter for a SpeechLine subscription.
#
# Liveness: the receiver has no /osc/ping, so the probe asks the product name,
# a fixed question every unit answers; any reply counts, an error included.
#
# Format: YAML. Every address is a fixed JSON string, every value a json: true
# rule, and the subscriptions are queries like any other.
#
# NOT hardware-verified. Built from the document and its own examples.

id: sennheiser_sl_rack_receiver_dw
name: Sennheiser SpeechLine SL Rack Receiver DW
manufacturer: Sennheiser
category: audio
version: "1.0.0"
author: OpenAVC
min_platform_version: "0.37.0"
description: >
  Controls the Sennheiser SpeechLine SL Rack Receiver DW, the single-channel
  SpeechLine Digital Wireless receiver, over Sennheiser Sound Control (JSON
  over UDP, port 45). Mute and mute mode, output level, EQ preset and low
  cut, pairing, walk test and identify, the linked transmitter's type,
  capsule, battery, charging, sensitivity, locks and LED, RF quality and
  warnings, names, display brightness and restart. State is push-driven: the
  driver subscribes and the receiver reports every change as it happens,
  including changes made on the receiver, in Control Cockpit or on a
  transmitter.

source_url: https://assets.sennheiser.com/download/assets/TI_1094_v4.3_Sennheiser_Sound_Control_Protocol_SL_DW_EN.pdf/b2a3c92ce7bb11f088db768ee8e97aea
tags: [wireless, microphone, receiver, speechline, ssc]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [sennheiser_ssc]
ports: [45]

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Sennheiser
    models: [SL Rack Receiver DW]
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Built from Sennheiser's SSC developer guide for firmware 4.1.1; not yet
      run against a receiver. The SL MCR 2 / 4 DW multi-channel receivers and
      the CHG 2N / 4N chargers use different SSC commands and have their own
      drivers. Network address configuration and firmware updates belong to
      Sennheiser Control Cockpit.

transport: udp

help:
  overview: >
    Controls the Sennheiser SpeechLine SL Rack Receiver DW: mute it, choose
    what the transmitter's mute switch does, set its output level, EQ preset
    and low cut, pair a transmitter, run a walk test, and read the linked
    transmitter's type, capsule, battery and warnings. Everything that
    changes on the receiver, in Control Cockpit or on a transmitter shows up
    here as it happens.
  setup: >
    1. Give the receiver a static IP address or a DHCP reservation, and note
       it.
    2. Enter that address here. Control uses UDP port 45; leave the port
       alone.
    3. The audio level meter is off by default. It makes the receiver stream
       continuously, so turn on Enable Level Meter only when a panel shows
       it. The Meter On and Meter Off commands switch it while running.
    4. The receiver and the OpenAVC server must be able to exchange UDP
       traffic on port 45 in both directions. If the receiver shows offline
       while Control Cockpit still sees it, check for a firewall between the
       two.
  connection: >
    The receiver answers on UDP port 45. If Control Cockpit sees it and
    OpenAVC does not, a firewall between the server and the receiver is
    blocking UDP 45.

discovery:
  # The SL Rack Receiver DW reports the bare product name "SLDW" (§8.18); the
  # SL MCR DW reports "SLDW" with a channel count after it ("SLDW4CH"), which
  # the closing quote here leaves out. Every SSC device answers UDP 45, so the
  # port alone proves nothing.
  udp_probe:
    port: 45
    send_ascii: '{"device":{"identity":{"product":null}}}'
    expect_regex: '"product"\s*:\s*"SLDW"'
    timeout_ms: 1500
    extract:
      model:
        regex: '"product"\s*:\s*"(SLDW)"'
        group: 1
    extract_manufacturer: "Sennheiser"
  oui:
    - "00:1b:66"   # Sennheiser electronic GmbH & Co. KG
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "sennheiser"

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 45
  poll_interval: 30
  # The document states no minimum gap between messages; this is the
  # platform's default. Connect sends about fifty messages, one address each.
  inter_command_delay: 0.05
  enable_level_meter: false

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: IP Address
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 45
    label: UDP Port
    help: "Sennheiser Sound Control listens on UDP port 45."
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 30
    min: 5
    # Each subscription lives 90 s; at 30 s or less every one is renewed at
    # least twice before it would end.
    max: 30
    label: Poll Interval (sec)
    help: >
      How often the subscriptions are renewed, which also re-reads every
      value. The receiver reports changes as they happen, so 30 s is plenty.
  inter_command_delay:
    type: number
    default: 0.05
    min: 0
    label: Inter-Command Delay (sec)
    help: "Pause between messages sent to the receiver."
  enable_level_meter:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Enable Level Meter
    help: >
      Stream the receiver's output level into OpenAVC (Audio Level). The
      receiver sends it continuously once enabled, so leave it off unless a
      panel shows it.

liveness:
  send: '{"device":{"identity":{"product":null}}}'
  # Any answer proves the receiver is there, a refusal included.
  expect: '"product"|"error"'
  interval: 20
  timeout: 5
  max_failures: 2

# Reads first (none of these can be subscribed), then one subscription per
# address. Each subscription is written once here, with an anchor; the poll
# and the two rules that subscribe again below reuse the same entries.
on_connect:
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"product":null}}}'
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"version":null}}}'
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"serial":null}}}'
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"vendor":null}}}'
  - '{"interface":{"version":null}}'
  - '{"device":{"network":{"ether":{"macs":null}}}}'
  - '{"device":{"network":{"ipv4":{"ipaddr":null}}}}'
  # ── The receiver ──
  - &sub_name { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"name":null}}]}}}', query_for: device_name }
  - &sub_group { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"group":null}}]}}}', query_for: group }
  - &sub_location { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"location":null}}]}}}', query_for: location }
  - &sub_mdns { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"network":{"mdns_responder":null}}}]}}}', query_for: mdns_enabled }
  - &sub_state { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"state":null}}]}}}', query_for: device_state }
  # Pre-condition: pairing or an update running (§8.36).
  - &sub_progress { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"progress":null}}]}}}', when_state: { device_state: [pairing, receiver_update, transmitter_update] }, query_for: progress }
  - &sub_brightness { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"brightness":null}]}}}', query_for: display_brightness }
  # ── The channel ──
  - &sub_identify { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"identify":null}}]}}}', query_for: identifying }
  - &sub_pair { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"pair":null}}]}}}', query_for: pairing }
  - &sub_rf_quality { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"rf_quality":null}}]}}}', query_for: rf_quality_percent }
  - &sub_walktest { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"walktest":null}}]}}}', query_for: walktest }
  - &sub_mute_switch { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"mute_switch_active":null}}]}}}', query_for: mute_switch_active }
  - &sub_sync { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"sync_info":null}}]}}}', query_for: sync_info }
  - &sub_rfpi { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"rfpi":null}}]}}}', query_for: rfpi }
  - &sub_ipei { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"last_paired_ipei":null}}]}}}', query_for: last_paired_ipei }
  - &sub_autolock { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"autolock":null}}]}}}', query_for: autolock }
  - &sub_rx_warnings { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"warnings":null}}]}}}', query_for: bad_link }
  - &sub_mute_mode { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"mute_mode":null}}]}}}', query_for: mute_mode }
  - &sub_mute { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"rx1":{"mute_state":null}}]}}}', query_for: mute }
  - &sub_gain { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"audio":{"out1":{"gain_db":null}}}]}}}', query_for: gain }
  - &sub_eq { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":null}}}]}}}', query_for: eq_preset }
  - &sub_low_cut { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"audio":{"low_cut":null}}]}}}', query_for: low_cut }
  # ── The transmitter: link, and the settings the receiver keeps ──
  - &sub_active { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"active":null}}]}}}', query_for: tx_linked }
  - &sub_agc { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":null}}}]}}}', query_for: tx_sensitivity }
  - &sub_auto_off { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"auto_power_off":null}}}]}}}', query_for: tx_auto_power_off }
  # ── The linked transmitter (pre-condition: a link, §8.53-8.72) ──
  # Not subscribable: read once a link is known.
  - &read_switch_label { send: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"switch1":{"label":null}}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_switch_label }
  - &sub_tx_type { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"device_type":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_type }
  - &sub_bat_type { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_type":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_battery_type }
  - &sub_bat_gauge { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_gauge":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_battery_percent }
  - &sub_bat_lifetime { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_lifetime":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_battery_minutes }
  - &sub_bat_bars { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_bars":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_battery_bars }
  - &sub_bat_health { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_health":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_battery_health_percent }
  - &sub_bat_cycles { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_cycles":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_battery_cycles }
  - &sub_bat_charging { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_charging":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_charging }
  - &sub_switch { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"switch1":{"state":null}}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_switch_state }
  - &sub_acoustic { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"acoustic":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_capsule }
  - &sub_tx_warnings { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"warnings":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_low_battery }
  - &sub_gooseneck { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"gooseneck_state":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_gooseneck_attached }
  - &sub_power_lock { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"power_lock":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_power_lock }
  - &sub_pairing_lock { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"pairing_lock":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_pairing_lock }
  - &sub_led { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"mates":{"tx1":{"led_active":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { tx_linked: true }, query_for: tx_led }
  # ── Level meter (opt-in) ──
  - send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"audio":{"out1":{"level_db":null}}}]}}}'
    when: enable_level_meter
    query_for: level_dbfs

# Renew every subscription each cycle: a renewal is the same request as the
# first one (§5.1) and its answer carries the current value.
polling:
  queries:
    - *sub_name
    - *sub_group
    - *sub_location
    - *sub_mdns
    - *sub_state
    - *sub_progress
    - *sub_brightness
    - *sub_identify
    - *sub_pair
    - *sub_rf_quality
    - *sub_walktest
    - *sub_mute_switch
    - *sub_sync
    - *sub_rfpi
    - *sub_ipei
    - *sub_autolock
    - *sub_rx_warnings
    - *sub_mute_mode
    - *sub_mute
    - *sub_gain
    - *sub_eq
    - *sub_low_cut
    - *sub_active
    - *sub_agc
    - *sub_auto_off
    - *sub_tx_type
    - *sub_bat_type
    - *sub_bat_gauge
    - *sub_bat_lifetime
    - *sub_bat_bars
    - *sub_bat_health
    - *sub_bat_cycles
    - *sub_bat_charging
    - *sub_switch
    - *sub_acoustic
    - *sub_tx_warnings
    - *sub_gooseneck
    - *sub_power_lock
    - *sub_pairing_lock
    - *sub_led
    # Not subscribable: read each cycle, so a transmitter that links between
    # connects shows its label on a release without then_query too.
    - *read_switch_label
    # The meter is renewed while the receiver confirmed it on (Meter On, or
    # Enable Level Meter at connect), and not after Meter Off.
    - &sub_meter { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"audio":{"out1":{"level_db":null}}}]}}}', when_state: { metering: true }, query_for: level_dbfs }

state_variables:
  # ── Identity and network ──
  model:
    type: string
    label: Model
    help: "The receiver's product name (SLDW)."
  firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: Firmware Version
  serial_number:
    type: string
    label: Serial Number
  vendor:
    type: string
    label: Vendor
  interface_version:
    type: string
    label: SSC Interface Version
  mac_address:
    type: string
    label: MAC Address
  ip_address:
    type: string
    label: IP Address
  mdns_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: mDNS
    help: "The receiver announces itself for discovery (takes effect after a restart)."
  # ── Names ──
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: Device Name
    help: "The receiver's name, as shown in Control Cockpit and in device discovery."
  group:
    type: string
    label: Group
    help: "The receiver's group name, its Location menu item: up to 8 letters, digits, - and _."
  location:
    type: string
    label: Location
  # ── Receiver ──
  device_state:
    type: enum
    values: [normal, pairing, receiver_update, transmitter_update, transmitter_update_confirmation, transmitter_update_failed]
    label: Receiver State
    cloud_priority: high
    help: >
      normal; pairing; receiver_update (the receiver's firmware is updating);
      transmitter_update (the transmitter's firmware is updating);
      transmitter_update_confirmation (an update is waiting: Approve or
      Reject it); transmitter_update_failed.
  progress:
    type: integer
    label: Progress
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
    help: "The progress bar the receiver shows while pairing or updating."
  display_brightness:
    type: integer
    label: Display Brightness
    min: 0
    max: 100
    step: 1
    unit: "%"
  identifying:
    type: boolean
    label: Identifying
    help: "The receiver is flashing to show which unit it is."
  pairing:
    type: boolean
    label: Pairing
    help: "The receiver is waiting for a transmitter to pair."
  walktest:
    type: boolean
    label: Walk Test
  rf_quality_percent:
    type: integer
    label: RF Quality
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
    cloud_priority: low
  sync_info:
    type: enum
    values: [unknown, master, follower, unsynced_follower]
    label: Sync
    help: "How the receiver is synchronized: unknown, master, follower, or unsynced_follower (it lost its master)."
  rfpi:
    type: string
    label: RFPI
    help: "The receiver's radio identity."
  last_paired_ipei:
    type: string
    label: Last Paired Transmitter
    help: "Radio identity (IPEI) of the last transmitter linked to the receiver."
  autolock:
    type: boolean
    label: Auto Lock
    help: "The receiver's controls lock by themselves (its Auto Lock menu item)."
  mute_switch_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Transmitter Mute Switch
    help: "The transmitter's mute switch works (its Mute Switch menu item)."
  hw_failure:
    type: boolean
    label: Hardware Failure
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "The receiver found a hardware failure when it started."
  bad_link:
    type: boolean
    label: Bad Link
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "The radio link to the transmitter is poor."
  no_fw_image:
    type: boolean
    label: No Transmitter Firmware
    help: "The receiver has no firmware image to update the linked transmitter with."
  link_disabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Link Disabled
    help: "The receiver's radio is switched off."
  # ── Audio ──
  mute:
    type: boolean
    label: Mute
    control: true
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "The receiver's mute, set from here or by the transmitter's mute switch."
  mute_mode:
    type: enum
    values: ["off", "on", push_to_talk, push_to_mute, room_mute]
    label: Mute Mode
    control: true
    help: >
      What the transmitter's mute switch does: off (no mute), on (the switch
      mutes), push_to_talk, push_to_mute, or room_mute (location-based mute).
  gain:
    type: integer
    label: Output Level
    min: -24
    max: 12
    step: 6
    unit: dB
    control: true
    # The receiver's own number is an index, 0 = -24 dB to 6 = +12 dB (§8.75).
    scale: 6
    offset: -24
    help: "The receiver's audio output level (its Audio Level menu item), -24 to +12 dB in 6 dB steps."
  eq_preset:
    type: enum
    values: ["off", female_speech, male_speech, media, custom]
    label: EQ Preset
    control: true
    help: "The receiver's sound profile."
  low_cut:
    type: boolean
    label: Low Cut
    control: true
  metering:
    type: boolean
    label: Metering
    help: "The receiver is streaming its audio level."
  level_dbfs:
    type: number
    label: Audio Level
    min: -60
    max: 0
    unit: dBFS
    cloud_priority: low
    help: "The receiver's output level, -60 to 0, while metering is on."
  # ── Transmitter ──
  tx_linked:
    type: boolean
    label: Transmitter Linked
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "A transmitter has a link to the receiver."
  no_link:
    type: boolean
    label: No Link
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "No transmitter is linked."
  tx_type:
    type: enum
    values: [handheld, bodypack, table_stand, boundary]
    label: Transmitter Type
  tx_capsule:
    type: string
    label: Capsule
    help: "The microphone or input of the linked transmitter (MD42, MME865, GOOSENECK and so on); INCOMPATIBLE for an unsupported capsule, empty when none is connected."
  tx_battery_type:
    type: enum
    values: [battery, rechargeable]
    label: Battery Type
  tx_battery_percent:
    type: integer
    label: Battery Level
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "Charge of a rechargeable battery, or the voltage level of a primary battery."
  tx_battery_minutes:
    type: integer
    label: Battery Runtime
    unit: min
    cloud_priority: high
    # The receiver reports seconds (§8.58).
    scale: 0.016666666666666666
    help: "Estimated runtime left on a rechargeable battery; not known for a while after power-on."
  tx_battery_bars:
    type: integer
    label: Battery Bars
    min: 0
    max: 5
    help: "Battery bars as the receiver shows them (rechargeable batteries)."
  tx_battery_health_percent:
    type: integer
    label: Battery Health
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
  tx_battery_cycles:
    type: integer
    label: Battery Cycles
  tx_charging:
    type: boolean
    label: Charging
    help: "A table-stand or boundary microphone's battery is charging."
  tx_gooseneck_attached:
    type: boolean
    label: Gooseneck Attached
    help: "A table-stand transmitter has its gooseneck attached."
  tx_switch_label:
    type: string
    label: Switch Label
    help: "The function of the transmitter's switch."
  tx_switch_state:
    type: boolean
    label: Transmitter Switch
    help: "The transmitter's switch (its mute switch) is on."
  tx_low_battery:
    type: boolean
    label: Low Battery
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "The transmitter reports a low battery."
  tx_sensitivity:
    type: enum
    values: [automatic, 0db, -6db, -12db, -18db, -24db, -30db]
    label: Transmitter Sensitivity
    control: true
    help: "Automatic gain control, or a fixed sensitivity (the Sensitivity menu item)."
  tx_auto_power_off:
    type: enum
    values: ["off", 10min, 20min, 30min]
    label: Transmitter Auto Power Off
    help: "The transmitter switches off after this long without a link."
  tx_power_lock:
    type: boolean
    label: Power Button Locked
  tx_pairing_lock:
    type: boolean
    label: Pairing Button Locked
  tx_led:
    type: boolean
    label: Transmitter LED
    help: "The LED of a handheld or bodypack transmitter is on."
  # ── Errors ──
  last_error:
    type: string
    label: Last Error
    help: "What the receiver said about the last request it did not accept."
  last_error_code:
    type: integer
    label: Last Error Code

commands:
  # ── Mute ──
  mute_on:
    label: Mute
    help: "Mutes the receiver."
    send: '{"rx1":{"mute_state":true}}'
    sets: { mute: true }
  mute_off:
    label: Unmute
    help: "Unmutes the receiver."
    send: '{"rx1":{"mute_state":false}}'
    sets: { mute: false }
  set_mute_mode:
    label: Set Mute Mode
    help: "Chooses what the transmitter's mute switch does."
    send: '{"rx1":{"mute_mode":{mode}}}'
    sets: { mute_mode: "{mode}" }
    params:
      mode:
        type: enum
        values: ["off", "on", push_to_talk, push_to_mute, room_mute]
        required: true
        label: Mute Mode
        map: { "off": "0", "on": "1", "push_to_talk": "2", "push_to_mute": "3", "room_mute": "4" }

  # ── Audio ──
  set_gain:
    label: Set Output Level
    help: "Sets the receiver's audio output level, -24 to +12 dB in 6 dB steps; a value between steps goes to the nearest one."
    send: '{"audio":{"out1":{"gain_db":{gain}}}}'
    sets: { gain: "{gain}" }
    params:
      gain:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Level
        min: -24
        max: 12
        unit: dB
        scale: 6
        offset: -24
  set_eq_preset:
    label: Set EQ Preset
    help: "Chooses the receiver's sound profile."
    send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":{preset}}}}'
    sets: { eq_preset: "{preset}" }
    params:
      preset:
        type: enum
        values: ["off", female_speech, male_speech, media, custom]
        required: true
        label: Preset
        map: { "off": "0", "female_speech": "1", "male_speech": "2", "media": "3", "custom": "4" }
  low_cut_on:
    label: Low Cut On
    help: "Switches the low-cut filter on."
    send: '{"audio":{"low_cut":true}}'
    sets: { low_cut: true }
  low_cut_off:
    label: Low Cut Off
    help: "Switches the low-cut filter off."
    send: '{"audio":{"low_cut":false}}'
    sets: { low_cut: false }
  set_tx_sensitivity:
    label: Set Transmitter Sensitivity
    help: "Sets the transmitter's sensitivity: automatic gain control, or a fixed level."
    send: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":{sensitivity}}}}'
    sets: { tx_sensitivity: "{sensitivity}" }
    params:
      sensitivity:
        type: enum
        values: [automatic, 0db, -6db, -12db, -18db, -24db, -30db]
        required: true
        label: Sensitivity
        map: { "automatic": "0", "0db": "1", "-6db": "2", "-12db": "3", "-18db": "4", "-24db": "5", "-30db": "6" }

  # ── Level meter ──
  meter_on:
    label: Meter On
    help: "Starts the receiver streaming its audio level into Audio Level."
    send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"audio":{"out1":{"level_db":null}}}]}}}'
    sets: { metering: true }
  meter_off:
    label: Meter Off
    help: "Stops the audio level stream."
    send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"cancel":true},"audio":{"out1":{"level_db":null}}}]}}}'
    sets: { metering: false }

  # ── Pairing, walk test, identify ──
  identify:
    label: Identify Receiver
    help: "Flashes the receiver so it can be found in the rack. Not while pairing or in a walk test."
    send: '{"rx1":{"identify":true}}'
    sets: { identifying: true }
  identify_off:
    label: Stop Identifying
    help: "Stops the receiver flashing."
    send: '{"rx1":{"identify":false}}'
    sets: { identifying: false }
  start_pairing:
    label: Start Pairing
    help: "Puts the receiver in pairing mode, so a transmitter in pairing mode links to it. Not during a walk test."
    send: '{"rx1":{"pair":true}}'
    sets: { pairing: true }
  stop_pairing:
    label: Stop Pairing
    help: "Ends pairing mode."
    send: '{"rx1":{"pair":false}}'
    sets: { pairing: false }
  walktest_on:
    label: Start Walk Test
    help: "Starts a walk test: the receiver reports the link quality while someone walks the room with the transmitter. Not while pairing or identifying."
    send: '{"rx1":{"walktest":true}}'
    sets: { walktest: true }
  walktest_off:
    label: Stop Walk Test
    help: "Ends the walk test."
    send: '{"rx1":{"walktest":false}}'
    sets: { walktest: false }

  # ── Transmitter ──
  power_down_tx:
    label: Switch Off Transmitter
    help: "Switches the linked transmitter off. Its audio stops until someone switches it on again."
    send: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"power_down":true}}}'
    confirm: "Switches the linked transmitter off. It can only be switched on again at the transmitter."
  approve_tx_update:
    label: Approve Transmitter Update
    help: "Lets the receiver update the linked transmitter's firmware, while Receiver State is transmitter_update_confirmation."
    send: '{"device":{"update":{"confirmation":true}}}'
  reject_tx_update:
    label: Reject Transmitter Update
    help: "Declines the waiting transmitter firmware update."
    send: '{"device":{"update":{"confirmation":false}}}'

  # ── Receiver ──
  restart:
    label: Restart Receiver
    help: "Restarts the receiver. Its audio stops until it is back."
    send: '{"device":{"reset":true}}'
    confirm: "Restarts the receiver. Its audio stops until it is back."
    # The document gives no boot time; not yet measured on a unit.
    restarts_device_for: 90
  factory_reset:
    label: Factory Reset
    help: "Returns every setting on the receiver to its factory default and restarts it."
    send: '{"device":{"factory_reset":true}}'
    confirm: "Returns every setting on the receiver to its factory default, its name and network settings included, and restarts it."
    restarts_device_for: 90
  restore_audio_defaults:
    label: Reset Audio Effects
    help: "Restores the receiver's audio effects to their defaults, as its Effects Reset menu item does."
    send: '{"audio":{"effects_reset":true}}'
    confirm: "Restores the receiver's audio effects to their defaults."

quick_actions: [mute_on, mute_off, identify]

actions:
  - id: mute_on
    icon: mic-off
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.mute", operator: falsy }
  - id: mute_off
    icon: mic
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.mute", operator: truthy }
  - id: identify
    icon: sun

device_settings:
  # ── Names ──
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: Device Name
    help: "The receiver's name in Control Cockpit and in discovery. No double quotes or backslashes."
    state_key: device_name
    default: "SLDW"
    regex: '^[^"\\]{1,64}$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"name":"{value}"}}'
  group:
    type: string
    label: Group
    help: "Up to 8 letters, digits, - and _, starting with a letter and ending with a letter or digit."
    state_key: group
    default: ""
    regex: '^(?:[A-Za-z](?:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,6}[A-Za-z0-9])?)?$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"group":"{value}"}}'
  location:
    type: string
    label: Location
    help: "Where the receiver is. No double quotes or backslashes."
    state_key: location
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"\\]{0,64}$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"location":"{value}"}}'
  display_brightness:
    type: integer
    label: Display Brightness (%)
    state_key: display_brightness
    default: 100
    min: 0
    max: 100
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"brightness":{value}}'
  mdns_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: mDNS
    help: "The receiver announces itself for discovery. Takes effect after the receiver restarts."
    state_key: mdns_enabled
    default: true
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"network":{"mdns_responder":{value}}}}'
  autolock:
    type: boolean
    label: Auto Lock
    help: "The receiver's controls lock by themselves."
    state_key: autolock
    default: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"rx1":{"autolock":{value}}}'
  # ── Audio ──
  mute_mode:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "off", label: "Off (no mute)" }
      - { value: "on", label: "On (the switch mutes)" }
      - { value: push_to_talk, label: Push to talk }
      - { value: push_to_mute, label: Push to mute }
      - { value: room_mute, label: Location-based mute }
    label: Mute Mode
    state_key: mute_mode
    default: "on"
    map: { "off": "0", "on": "1", "push_to_talk": "2", "push_to_mute": "3", "room_mute": "4" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"rx1":{"mute_mode":{value}}}'
  mute_switch_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Transmitter Mute Switch
    help: "The transmitter's mute switch works."
    state_key: mute_switch_active
    default: true
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"rx1":{"mute_switch_active":{value}}}'
  gain:
    type: integer
    label: Output Level (dB)
    help: "-24 to +12 dB in 6 dB steps; a value between steps goes to the nearest one."
    state_key: gain
    default: 0
    min: -24
    max: 12
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"out1":{"gain_db":{value}}}}'
  eq_preset:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "off", label: "Off" }
      - { value: female_speech, label: Female speech }
      - { value: male_speech, label: Male speech }
      - { value: media, label: Media }
      - { value: custom, label: Custom }
    label: EQ Preset
    state_key: eq_preset
    default: "off"
    map: { "off": "0", "female_speech": "1", "male_speech": "2", "media": "3", "custom": "4" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":{value}}}}'
  low_cut:
    type: boolean
    label: Low Cut
    state_key: low_cut
    default: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"low_cut":{value}}}'
  # ── Transmitter (kept by the receiver; the locks and LED need a link) ──
  tx_sensitivity:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: automatic, label: Automatic }
      - { value: 0db, label: "0 dB" }
      - { value: -6db, label: "-6 dB" }
      - { value: -12db, label: "-12 dB" }
      - { value: -18db, label: "-18 dB" }
      - { value: -24db, label: "-24 dB" }
      - { value: -30db, label: "-30 dB" }
    label: Transmitter Sensitivity
    state_key: tx_sensitivity
    default: automatic
    map: { "automatic": "0", "0db": "1", "-6db": "2", "-12db": "3", "-18db": "4", "-24db": "5", "-30db": "6" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":{value}}}}'
  tx_auto_power_off:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "off", label: "Off" }
      - { value: 10min, label: "After 10 minutes" }
      - { value: 20min, label: "After 20 minutes" }
      - { value: 30min, label: "After 30 minutes" }
    label: Transmitter Auto Power Off
    help: "The transmitter switches off after this long without a link."
    state_key: tx_auto_power_off
    default: "off"
    map: { "off": "0", "10min": "1", "20min": "2", "30min": "3" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"auto_power_off":{value}}}}'
  tx_power_lock:
    type: boolean
    label: Power Button Locked
    help: "The transmitter's power button does nothing. Needs a linked transmitter."
    state_key: tx_power_lock
    default: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"power_lock":{value}}}}'
  tx_pairing_lock:
    type: boolean
    label: Pairing Button Locked
    help: "The transmitter's pairing button does nothing. Needs a linked transmitter."
    state_key: tx_pairing_lock
    default: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"pairing_lock":{value}}}}'
  tx_led:
    type: boolean
    label: Transmitter LED
    help: "The LED of a handheld or bodypack transmitter is on. Needs a linked transmitter."
    state_key: tx_led
    default: true
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"led_active":{value}}}}'

responses:
  # ── Every value the receiver reports ──
  # Each answer and notification is an address tree; a body without a key
  # leaves that key's variable alone.
  - json: true
    set:
      model: device.identity.product
      firmware_version: device.identity.version
      serial_number: device.identity.serial
      vendor: device.identity.vendor
      interface_version: interface.version
      mac_address: device.network.ether.macs.0
      ip_address: device.network.ipv4.ipaddr.0
      mdns_enabled: device.network.mdns_responder
      device_name: device.name
      group: device.group
      location: device.location
      device_state:
        key: device.state
        map: { "0": normal, "1": pairing, "2": receiver_update, "3": transmitter_update, "4": transmitter_update_confirmation, "5": transmitter_update_failed }
      progress: device.progress
      display_brightness: brightness
      identifying: rx1.identify
      pairing: rx1.pair
      rf_quality_percent: rx1.rf_quality
      walktest: rx1.walktest
      mute_switch_active: rx1.mute_switch_active
      sync_info:
        key: rx1.sync_info
        map: { "0": unknown, "1": master, "2": follower, "3": unsynced_follower }
      rfpi: rx1.rfpi
      last_paired_ipei: rx1.last_paired_ipei
      autolock: rx1.autolock
      # A list of warning names (§8.49); one flag each.
      hw_failure: { key: rx1.warnings, contains: "HW Failure" }
      bad_link: { key: rx1.warnings, contains: "Bad Link" }
      no_fw_image: { key: rx1.warnings, contains: "No FW Image" }
      link_disabled: { key: rx1.warnings, contains: "Link Disabled" }
      mute_mode:
        key: rx1.mute_mode
        map: { "0": "off", "1": "on", "2": push_to_talk, "3": push_to_mute, "4": room_mute }
      mute: rx1.mute_state
      gain: audio.out1.gain_db
      eq_preset:
        key: audio.equalizer.preset
        map: { "0": "off", "1": female_speech, "2": male_speech, "3": media, "4": custom }
      low_cut: audio.low_cut
      tx_sensitivity:
        key: mates.tx1.agc
        map: { "0": automatic, "1": 0db, "2": -6db, "3": -12db, "4": -18db, "5": -24db, "6": -30db }
      # The document's example answers "1" (a string) where the type is a
      # number; either reads the same here.
      tx_auto_power_off:
        key: mates.tx1.auto_power_off
        map: { "0": "off", "1": 10min, "2": 20min, "3": 30min }
      tx_type:
        key: mates.tx1.device_type
        map: { "0": handheld, "1": bodypack, "2": table_stand, "3": boundary }
      tx_battery_type:
        key: mates.tx1.bat_type
        map: { "0": battery, "1": rechargeable }
      tx_battery_percent: mates.tx1.bat_gauge
      tx_battery_minutes: mates.tx1.bat_lifetime
      tx_battery_bars: mates.tx1.bat_bars
      tx_battery_health_percent: mates.tx1.bat_health
      tx_battery_cycles: mates.tx1.bat_cycles
      tx_charging: mates.tx1.bat_charging
      tx_gooseneck_attached: mates.tx1.gooseneck_state
      tx_switch_label: mates.tx1.switch1.label
      tx_switch_state: mates.tx1.switch1.state
      tx_capsule: mates.tx1.acoustic
      tx_low_battery: { key: mates.tx1.warnings, contains: "Low Bat" }
      tx_power_lock: mates.tx1.power_lock
      tx_pairing_lock: mates.tx1.pairing_lock
      tx_led: mates.tx1.led_active

  # ── Level meter: a continuous feed while subscribed ──
  # The throttle writes the newest frame when each window ends, so the last
  # level of a burst is never lost.
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.25
    set:
      level_dbfs: audio.out1.level_db

  # Every rule below reads text, and each may meet a reply the json rules
  # above also read (a subscription's answer can carry its current value), so
  # every one stays eligible past them (after_json). The first that matches
  # wins.

  # ── A subscription ended (310, §5.1): subscribe everything again ──
  # The poll would renew it within 30 s; this does it at once. Reading the
  # text also catches the document's own 310 examples, which are not valid
  # JSON.
  - match: '"error"\s*:.*?\[\s*310\b'
    after_json: true
    set: {}
    then_query:
      - *sub_name
      - *sub_group
      - *sub_location
      - *sub_mdns
      - *sub_state
      - *sub_progress
      - *sub_brightness
      - *sub_identify
      - *sub_pair
      - *sub_rf_quality
      - *sub_walktest
      - *sub_mute_switch
      - *sub_sync
      - *sub_rfpi
      - *sub_ipei
      - *sub_autolock
      - *sub_rx_warnings
      - *sub_mute_mode
      - *sub_mute
      - *sub_gain
      - *sub_eq
      - *sub_low_cut
      - *sub_active
      - *sub_agc
      - *sub_auto_off
      - *sub_tx_type
      - *sub_bat_type
      - *sub_bat_gauge
      - *sub_bat_lifetime
      - *sub_bat_bars
      - *sub_bat_health
      - *sub_bat_cycles
      - *sub_bat_charging
      - *sub_switch
      - *sub_acoustic
      - *sub_tx_warnings
      - *sub_gooseneck
      - *sub_power_lock
      - *sub_pairing_lock
      - *sub_led
      - *sub_meter

  # ── A refused read or subscription of a value the driver never writes ──
  # The linked transmitter's values need a link, battery runtime, bars,
  # health and cycles a rechargeable battery, charging a table-stand or
  # boundary on one, the gooseneck a table-stand, and the progress bar
  # pairing or an update. The driver never writes any of these, so a refusal
  # of one answers a read or a subscription (the link can drop between two
  # messages) and is not an error to show. The transmitter settings the
  # driver writes (its locks and LED) are not listed: their refusal is.
  - match: '"error"\s*:.*?"(?:device_type|bat_type|bat_gauge|bat_lifetime|bat_bars|bat_health|bat_cycles|bat_charging|label|state|acoustic|warnings|gooseneck_state|progress)"\s*:\s*\[\s*\d{3}'
    after_json: true
    set: {}

  # ── Any other refusal (§8.4, §9) ──
  # {"osc":{"error":[{"rx1":{"mute_mode":[406]}}]}}, or [400] for a message
  # the receiver could not read; a "desc" may follow the code.
  - match: '"error"\s*:.*?\[\s*(\d{3})\b'
    after_json: true
    mappings:
      - { group: 1, state: last_error_code, type: integer }
      - group: 1
        state: last_error
        map:
          "400": "The receiver could not read the request (400)."
          "403": "The receiver refused the request (403)."
          "404": "The receiver has no such setting (404)."
          "406": "The receiver did not accept the value, or cannot change it now (406)."
          "409": "The request conflicts with the receiver's current state (409)."
          "413": "The request was too large for the receiver (413)."
          "414": "The request was too complex for the receiver (414)."
          "422": "The receiver could not carry out the request (422)."
          "423": "The setting is locked on the receiver (423)."
          "450": "The receiver's answer would be too long (450)."
          "454": "The receiver keeps that setting hidden (454)."
          "500": "The receiver had an internal error (500)."
          "501": "The receiver does not support that request (501)."
          "503": "The receiver is busy (503)."

  # ── The level meter, as the receiver confirmed it (the subscription echo) ──
  - match: '"subscribe"\s*:.*"cancel"\s*:\s*true.*"level_db"'
    after_json: true
    set: { metering: "false" }
  - match: '"subscribe"\s*:.*"lifetime".*"level_db"\s*:\s*null'
    after_json: true
    set: { metering: "true" }

  # ── The transmitter link (/mates/active, §8.52) ──
  # A link where there was none: subscribe the linked transmitter's values at
  # once (the poll subscribes them too, on releases without then_query).
  - match: '"mates"\s*:\s*\{\s*"active"\s*:\s*\[\s*"tx1"'
    after_json: true
    only_when: { key: tx_linked, operator: falsy }
    set: { tx_linked: "true", no_link: "false" }
    then_query:
      - *read_switch_label
      - *sub_tx_type
      - *sub_bat_type
      - *sub_bat_gauge
      - *sub_bat_lifetime
      - *sub_bat_bars
      - *sub_bat_health
      - *sub_bat_cycles
      - *sub_bat_charging
      - *sub_switch
      - *sub_acoustic
      - *sub_tx_warnings
      - *sub_gooseneck
      - *sub_power_lock
      - *sub_pairing_lock
      - *sub_led
  # Still linked (every renewal answers with the current list).
  - match: '"mates"\s*:\s*\{\s*"active"\s*:\s*\[\s*"tx1"'
    after_json: true
    set: { tx_linked: "true", no_link: "false" }
  # No link: clear what only a linked transmitter reports. Sensitivity and
  # auto power off stay, as the receiver keeps them.
  - match: '"mates"\s*:\s*\{\s*"active"\s*:\s*\[\s*\]'
    after_json: true
    set:
      tx_linked: "false"
      no_link: "true"
      tx_type: null
      tx_capsule: null
      tx_battery_type: null
      tx_battery_percent: null
      tx_battery_minutes: null
      tx_battery_bars: null
      tx_battery_health_percent: null
      tx_battery_cycles: null
      tx_charging: null
      tx_gooseneck_attached: null
      tx_switch_label: null
      tx_switch_state: null
      tx_low_battery: null
      tx_power_lock: null
      tx_pairing_lock: null
      tx_led: null

  # ── Pairing or an update started: its progress bar can be subscribed now ──
  - match: '"device"\s*:\s*\{\s*"state"\s*:\s*[123]\b'
    after_json: true
    set: {}
    then_query:
      - *sub_progress

  # ── A subscription's own answer ── carries nothing the rules above have not
  # read; acknowledged here so it does not count as a reply nobody read.
  - match: '"osc"\s*:\s*\{\s*"state"\s*:\s*\{\s*"subscribe"'
    after_json: true
    set: {}

# ── SIMULATOR ──
# One script handler is the whole SSC server: it parses the incoming JSON
# object, walks the address tree against the method table below, answers
# every address with its value, records subscriptions and answers each with
# the current value bundled after the echo, and refuses what the document
# says the receiver refuses (404 for an unknown address, /osc/ping included;
# 406 for a write to a read-only address, a value off its range or a method
# whose pre-condition does not hold, such as a transmitter value with no
# transmitter linked). Every change also goes out as a notification through
# the notifications: map below, which is what the receiver does after it
# answers a set.
#
# Answers are written the way the document writes a bundle: one member per
# address, so a message that asks for several addresses under one name gets
# that name repeated (§8.11 example 3), and an /osc/xid beside another osc
# method repeats "osc" (example 1). The driver sends one address per message,
# so it never draws one; anything else that talks to this simulator does.
#
# Not modelled (the sandbox has no clock): a subscription's lifetime and its
# 1000-notification limit (the End Subscriptions control sends the 310 the
# receiver would), the pairing countdown, and the restart after Restart or
# Factory Reset. Notifications go out whether or not the address is
# subscribed, and a warning flag's notification lists only that warning.
simulator:
  initial_state:
    _subscriptions: ""
    end_subscriptions: false
    model: "SLDW"
    firmware_version: "4.1.1"
    serial_number: "1454100930"
    vendor: "Sennheiser electronic GmbH & Co. KG"
    interface_version: "1.2"
    mac_address: "00:1B:66:7D:F8:99"
    ip_address: "192.168.1.203"
    mdns_enabled: true
    device_name: "SLDW"
    group: "room"
    location: "Meeting Room A"
    device_state: "normal"
    progress: 0
    display_brightness: 75
    identifying: false
    pairing: false
    rf_quality_percent: 80
    walktest: false
    mute_switch_active: true
    sync_info: "master"
    rfpi: "028112cf28"
    last_paired_ipei: "028110a938"
    autolock: false
    hw_failure: false
    bad_link: false
    no_fw_image: false
    link_disabled: false
    mute_mode: "on"
    mute: false
    gain: 0
    eq_preset: "off"
    low_cut: false
    level_dbfs: -60
    tx_linked: true
    tx_type: "table_stand"
    tx_capsule: "GOOSENECK"
    tx_battery_type: "rechargeable"
    tx_battery_percent: 83
    tx_battery_minutes: 641
    tx_battery_bars: 4
    tx_battery_health_percent: 100
    tx_battery_cycles: 6
    tx_charging: false
    tx_gooseneck_attached: true
    tx_switch_label: "Mute"
    tx_switch_state: false
    tx_low_battery: false
    tx_sensitivity: "automatic"
    tx_auto_power_off: "off"
    tx_power_lock: false
    tx_pairing_lock: false
    tx_led: true

  delays:
    command_response: 0.02

  controls:
    - { type: toggle, key: tx_linked, label: Transmitter Linked }
    - { type: toggle, key: mute, label: Muted }
    - { type: select, key: mute_mode, label: Mute Mode, options: ["off", "on", push_to_talk, push_to_mute, room_mute] }
    - { type: slider, key: rf_quality_percent, label: RF Quality (%), min: 0, max: 100 }
    - { type: toggle, key: bad_link, label: Bad Link }
    - { type: toggle, key: hw_failure, label: Hardware Failure }
    - { type: select, key: tx_type, label: Transmitter Type, options: [handheld, bodypack, table_stand, boundary] }
    - { type: select, key: tx_battery_type, label: Battery Type, options: [battery, rechargeable] }
    - { type: slider, key: tx_battery_percent, label: Battery Level (%), min: 0, max: 100 }
    - { type: slider, key: tx_battery_minutes, label: Battery Runtime (min), min: 0, max: 900 }
    - { type: toggle, key: tx_low_battery, label: Low Battery }
    - { type: toggle, key: tx_charging, label: Charging }
    - { type: toggle, key: tx_switch_state, label: Transmitter Switch }
    - { type: select, key: device_state, label: Receiver State, options: [normal, pairing, receiver_update, transmitter_update, transmitter_update_confirmation, transmitter_update_failed] }
    - { type: slider, key: progress, label: Progress (%), min: 0, max: 100 }
    - { type: slider, key: level_dbfs, label: Audio Level (dBFS), min: -60, max: 0 }
    - { type: toggle, key: end_subscriptions, label: End Subscriptions (310) }

  # What the receiver sends, unasked, when a value changes. Booleans and the
  # numbered values need a template per value (the JSON literal); gain and
  # battery runtime go out in the receiver's own numbers (an index, seconds).
  notifications:
    device_name: '{"device":{"name":"{value}"}}'
    group: '{"device":{"group":"{value}"}}'
    location: '{"device":{"location":"{value}"}}'
    mdns_enabled:
      'true': '{"device":{"network":{"mdns_responder":true}}}'
      'false': '{"device":{"network":{"mdns_responder":false}}}'
    device_state:
      normal: '{"device":{"state":0}}'
      pairing: '{"device":{"state":1}}'
      receiver_update: '{"device":{"state":2}}'
      transmitter_update: '{"device":{"state":3}}'
      transmitter_update_confirmation: '{"device":{"state":4}}'
      transmitter_update_failed: '{"device":{"state":5}}'
    progress: '{"device":{"progress":{value}}}'
    display_brightness: '{"brightness":{value}}'
    identifying:
      'true': '{"rx1":{"identify":true}}'
      'false': '{"rx1":{"identify":false}}'
    pairing:
      'true': '{"rx1":{"pair":true}}'
      'false': '{"rx1":{"pair":false}}'
    rf_quality_percent: '{"rx1":{"rf_quality":{value}}}'
    walktest:
      'true': '{"rx1":{"walktest":true}}'
      'false': '{"rx1":{"walktest":false}}'
    mute_switch_active:
      'true': '{"rx1":{"mute_switch_active":true}}'
      'false': '{"rx1":{"mute_switch_active":false}}'
    sync_info:
      unknown: '{"rx1":{"sync_info":0}}'
      master: '{"rx1":{"sync_info":1}}'
      follower: '{"rx1":{"sync_info":2}}'
      unsynced_follower: '{"rx1":{"sync_info":3}}'
    autolock:
      'true': '{"rx1":{"autolock":true}}'
      'false': '{"rx1":{"autolock":false}}'
    hw_failure:
      'true': '{"rx1":{"warnings":["HW Failure"]}}'
      'false': '{"rx1":{"warnings":[]}}'
    bad_link:
      'true': '{"rx1":{"warnings":["Bad Link"]}}'
      'false': '{"rx1":{"warnings":[]}}'
    mute_mode:
      'off': '{"rx1":{"mute_mode":0}}'
      'on': '{"rx1":{"mute_mode":1}}'
      push_to_talk: '{"rx1":{"mute_mode":2}}'
      push_to_mute: '{"rx1":{"mute_mode":3}}'
      room_mute: '{"rx1":{"mute_mode":4}}'
    mute:
      'true': '{"rx1":{"mute_state":true}}'
      'false': '{"rx1":{"mute_state":false}}'
    gain: '{"audio":{"out1":{"gain_db":{value}}}}'
    eq_preset:
      'off': '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":0}}}'
      female_speech: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":1}}}'
      male_speech: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":2}}}'
      media: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":3}}}'
      custom: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":4}}}'
    low_cut:
      'true': '{"audio":{"low_cut":true}}'
      'false': '{"audio":{"low_cut":false}}'
    level_dbfs: '{"audio":{"out1":{"level_db":{value}}}}'
    tx_linked:
      'true': '{"mates":{"active":["tx1"]}}'
      'false': '{"mates":{"active":[]}}'
    tx_type:
      handheld: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"device_type":0}}}'
      bodypack: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"device_type":1}}}'
      table_stand: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"device_type":2}}}'
      boundary: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"device_type":3}}}'
    tx_battery_type:
      battery: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_type":0}}}'
      rechargeable: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_type":1}}}'
    tx_battery_percent: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_gauge":{value}}}}'
    tx_battery_minutes: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_lifetime":{value}}}}'
    tx_battery_bars: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_bars":{value}}}}'
    tx_battery_health_percent: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_health":{value}}}}'
    tx_battery_cycles: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_cycles":{value}}}}'
    tx_charging:
      'true': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_charging":true}}}'
      'false': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"bat_charging":false}}}'
    tx_gooseneck_attached:
      'true': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"gooseneck_state":true}}}'
      'false': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"gooseneck_state":false}}}'
    tx_switch_state:
      'true': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"switch1":{"state":true}}}}'
      'false': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"switch1":{"state":false}}}}'
    tx_capsule: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"acoustic":"{value}"}}}'
    tx_low_battery:
      'true': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"warnings":["Low Bat"]}}}'
      'false': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"warnings":[]}}}'
    tx_sensitivity:
      automatic: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":0}}}'
      0db: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":1}}}'
      -6db: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":2}}}'
      -12db: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":3}}}'
      -18db: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":4}}}'
      -24db: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":5}}}'
      -30db: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"agc":6}}}'
    tx_auto_power_off:
      'off': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"auto_power_off":0}}}'
      10min: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"auto_power_off":1}}}'
      20min: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"auto_power_off":2}}}'
      30min: '{"mates":{"tx1":{"auto_power_off":3}}}'
    tx_power_lock:
      'true': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"power_lock":true}}}'
      'false': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"power_lock":false}}}'
    tx_pairing_lock:
      'true': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"pairing_lock":true}}}'
      'false': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"pairing_lock":false}}}'
    tx_led:
      'true': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"led_active":true}}}'
      'false': '{"mates":{"tx1":{"led_active":false}}}'
    # The receiver's end of a subscription (§8.11), on demand.
    end_subscriptions:
      'true': '{"osc":{"error":[{"rx1":{"mute_state":[310]}}]}}'

  command_handlers:
    # Everything the socket receives goes through the one SSC server, so a
    # message that is not JSON gets the document's 400, not silence.
    - match: '(?s:.*)'
      handler: |
        def _run():
            text = match.group(0)

            # A whole float prints as an integer, as the receiver writes it.
            def plain(v):
                if v.__class__ is float and v == int(v):
                    return int(v)
                if v.__class__ is dict:
                    return {k: plain(x) for k, x in v.items()}
                if v.__class__ is list:
                    return [plain(x) for x in v]
                return v

            def dumps(v):
                return json.dumps(plain(v), separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False)

            MUTE_MODES = ["off", "on", "push_to_talk", "push_to_mute", "room_mute"]
            EQ = ["off", "female_speech", "male_speech", "media", "custom"]
            AGC = ["automatic", "0db", "-6db", "-12db", "-18db", "-24db", "-30db"]
            AUTO_OFF = ["off", "10min", "20min", "30min"]
            TX_TYPES = ["handheld", "bodypack", "table_stand", "boundary"]
            BAT_TYPES = ["battery", "rechargeable"]
            SYNC = ["unknown", "master", "follower", "unsynced_follower"]
            STATES = ["normal", "pairing", "receiver_update", "transmitter_update",
                      "transmitter_update_confirmation", "transmitter_update_failed"]

            # dotted address -> (kind, state key, extra, pre-condition, subscribable)
            # kinds: ro (read only), bool, int (lo, hi), idx (words: the
            # receiver's number is the index), str, gain (dB in state, index
            # 0-6 on the wire), seconds (minutes in state, seconds on the
            # wire), list1 (a one-element list), warn (flags -> names),
            # active (the link as a list), trigger (write only)
            LEAVES = {
                "interface.version": ("ro", "interface_version", None, None, False),
                "device.identity.product": ("ro", "model", None, None, False),
                "device.identity.version": ("ro", "firmware_version", None, None, False),
                "device.identity.serial": ("ro", "serial_number", None, None, False),
                "device.identity.vendor": ("ro", "vendor", None, None, False),
                "device.network.ether.macs": ("list1", "mac_address", None, None, False),
                "device.network.ipv4.ipaddr": ("list1", "ip_address", None, None, False),
                "device.network.mdns_responder": ("bool", "mdns_enabled", None, None, True),
                "device.name": ("str", "device_name", None, None, True),
                "device.group": ("str", "group", None, None, True),
                "device.location": ("str", "location", None, None, True),
                "device.state": ("ro_idx", "device_state", STATES, None, True),
                "device.progress": ("ro", "progress", None, "busy", True),
                "device.update.confirmation": ("confirm", None, None, "confirmation", False),
                "device.reset": ("trigger", None, None, None, False),
                "device.factory_reset": ("trigger", None, None, None, False),
                "brightness": ("int", "display_brightness", (0, 100), None, True),
                "rx1.identify": ("bool", "identifying", None, "not_pair_walk", True),
                "rx1.pair": ("pair", "pairing", None, "not_walk", True),
                "rx1.rf_quality": ("ro", "rf_quality_percent", None, None, True),
                "rx1.walktest": ("bool", "walktest", None, "not_pair_identify", True),
                "rx1.mute_switch_active": ("bool", "mute_switch_active", None, None, True),
                "rx1.sync_info": ("ro_idx", "sync_info", SYNC, None, True),
                "rx1.rfpi": ("ro", "rfpi", None, None, True),
                "rx1.last_paired_ipei": ("ro", "last_paired_ipei", None, None, True),
                "rx1.autolock": ("bool", "autolock", None, None, True),
                "rx1.warnings": ("warn", None, [("hw_failure", "HW Failure"), ("bad_link", "Bad Link"), ("no_fw_image", "No FW Image"), ("link_disabled", "Link Disabled")], None, True),
                "rx1.mute_mode": ("idx", "mute_mode", MUTE_MODES, None, True),
                "rx1.mute_state": ("bool", "mute", None, None, True),
                "mates.active": ("active", "tx_linked", None, None, True),
                "mates.tx1.device_type": ("ro_idx", "tx_type", TX_TYPES, "link", True),
                "mates.tx1.bat_type": ("ro_idx", "tx_battery_type", BAT_TYPES, "link", True),
                "mates.tx1.bat_charging": ("ro", "tx_charging", None, "charging", True),
                "mates.tx1.bat_gauge": ("ro", "tx_battery_percent", None, "link", True),
                "mates.tx1.bat_lifetime": ("seconds", "tx_battery_minutes", None, "recharge", True),
                "mates.tx1.bat_bars": ("ro", "tx_battery_bars", None, "recharge", True),
                "mates.tx1.bat_health": ("ro", "tx_battery_health_percent", None, "recharge", True),
                "mates.tx1.bat_cycles": ("ro", "tx_battery_cycles", None, "recharge", True),
                "mates.tx1.switch1.label": ("ro", "tx_switch_label", None, "link", False),
                "mates.tx1.switch1.state": ("ro", "tx_switch_state", None, "link", True),
                "mates.tx1.acoustic": ("ro", "tx_capsule", None, "link", True),
                "mates.tx1.warnings": ("warn", None, [("tx_low_battery", "Low Bat")], "link", True),
                "mates.tx1.gooseneck_state": ("ro", "tx_gooseneck_attached", None, "tablestand", True),
                "mates.tx1.agc": ("idx", "tx_sensitivity", AGC, None, True),
                "mates.tx1.power_lock": ("bool", "tx_power_lock", None, "link", True),
                "mates.tx1.power_down": ("power_down", None, None, "link", False),
                "mates.tx1.pairing_lock": ("bool", "tx_pairing_lock", None, "link", True),
                "mates.tx1.auto_power_off": ("idx", "tx_auto_power_off", AUTO_OFF, None, True),
                "mates.tx1.led_active": ("bool", "tx_led", None, "link", True),
                "audio.out1.label": ("label", None, None, None, False),
                "audio.out1.level_db": ("ro", "level_dbfs", None, None, True),
                "audio.out1.gain_db": ("gain", "gain", None, None, True),
                "audio.equalizer.preset": ("idx", "eq_preset", EQ, None, True),
                "audio.low_cut": ("bool", "low_cut", None, None, True),
                "audio.effects_reset": ("trigger", None, None, None, False),
            }
            OSC = {
                "osc.version": "1.0",
                "osc.feature.pattern": "*?",
                "osc.feature.baseaddr": False,
                "osc.feature.subscription": True,
                "osc.feature.timetag": False,
                "osc.state.prettyprint": False,
            }

            def holds(pre):
                if pre is None:
                    return True
                linked = bool(state["tx_linked"])
                if pre == "link":
                    return linked
                if pre == "recharge":
                    return linked and state["tx_battery_type"] == "rechargeable"
                if pre == "charging":
                    return (linked and state["tx_battery_type"] == "rechargeable"
                            and state["tx_type"] in ("table_stand", "boundary"))
                if pre == "tablestand":
                    return linked and state["tx_type"] == "table_stand"
                if pre == "busy":
                    return state["device_state"] in ("pairing", "receiver_update", "transmitter_update")
                if pre == "confirmation":
                    return state["device_state"] == "transmitter_update_confirmation"
                if pre == "not_pair_walk":
                    return not state["pairing"] and not state["walktest"]
                if pre == "not_walk":
                    return not state["walktest"]
                if pre == "not_pair_identify":
                    return not state["pairing"] and not state["identifying"]
                return True

            def current(spec):
                kind, key, extra = spec[0], spec[1], spec[2]
                if kind in ("idx", "ro_idx"):
                    word = state[key]
                    return extra.index(word) if word in extra else 0
                if kind == "gain":
                    return int((state[key] + 24) // 6)
                if kind == "seconds":
                    return int(state[key] * 60)
                if kind == "list1":
                    return [state[key]]
                if kind == "warn":
                    return [name for flag, name in extra if state[flag]]
                if kind == "active":
                    return ["tx1"] if state[key] else []
                if kind == "label":
                    return ["AF OUT BAL +18 dBu max", "AF OUT UNBAL"]
                if kind in ("trigger", "confirm", "power_down"):
                    return None
                return state[key]

            # A refused address is reported under osc.error and left out of
            # the answer; NO marks it.
            NO = ("refused",)

            def index_of(value, count):
                if value.__class__ is bool:
                    return None
                try:
                    n = int(value)
                except (TypeError, ValueError):
                    return None
                if n != float(value) or n < 0 or n >= count:
                    return None
                return n

            def apply(spec, value):
                # (result, error code)
                kind, key, extra = spec[0], spec[1], spec[2]
                if kind in ("ro", "ro_idx", "list1", "warn", "active", "label", "seconds"):
                    return NO, 406
                if kind == "bool":
                    if value.__class__ is not bool:
                        return NO, 406
                    state[key] = value
                    return value, 0
                if kind == "pair":
                    if value.__class__ is not bool:
                        return NO, 406
                    state[key] = value
                    if value:
                        state["progress"] = 0
                        state["device_state"] = "pairing"
                    elif state["device_state"] == "pairing":
                        state["device_state"] = "normal"
                    return value, 0
                if kind == "int":
                    n = index_of(value, extra[1] + 1)
                    if n is None or n < extra[0]:
                        return NO, 406
                    state[key] = n
                    return n, 0
                if kind == "idx":
                    n = index_of(value, len(extra))
                    if n is None:
                        return NO, 406
                    state[key] = extra[n]
                    return n, 0
                if kind == "gain":
                    n = index_of(value, 7)
                    if n is None:
                        return NO, 406
                    state[key] = n * 6 - 24
                    return n, 0
                if kind == "str":
                    if value.__class__ is not str:
                        return NO, 406
                    state[key] = value
                    return value, 0
                if kind == "trigger":
                    if value is not True:
                        return NO, 406
                    return True, 0
                if kind == "confirm":
                    if value.__class__ is not bool:
                        return NO, 406
                    state["progress"] = 0
                    state["device_state"] = "transmitter_update" if value else "normal"
                    return value, 0
                if kind == "power_down":
                    if value is not True:
                        return NO, 406
                    state["tx_linked"] = False
                    return True, 0
                return NO, 406

            members = []
            errors = []

            def tree(path, value):
                node = value
                for seg in path[::-1]:
                    node = {seg: node}
                return node

            def member(path, value):
                members.append(dumps(tree(path, value))[1:-1])

            def fail(path, code):
                errors.append(tree(path, [code]))

            def leaves_of(node, prefix):
                out = []
                for key, val in node.items():
                    if key == "#":
                        continue
                    path = prefix + [key]
                    dotted = ".".join(path)
                    if val.__class__ is dict and dotted not in LEAVES:
                        out.extend(leaves_of(val, path))
                    else:
                        out.append((path, val))
                return out

            def subscriptions():
                return [p for p in state["_subscriptions"].split(",") if p]

            def subscribe(value):
                if value is None:
                    tr = {}
                    for p in subscriptions():
                        node = tr
                        segs = p.split(".")
                        for seg in segs[:-1]:
                            node = node.setdefault(seg, {})
                        node[segs[-1]] = None
                    member(["osc", "state", "subscribe"], [tr])
                    return
                if value.__class__ is not list:
                    value = [value]
                subs = subscriptions()
                echoed = []
                initial = []
                for entry in value:
                    if entry.__class__ is not dict:
                        continue
                    params = entry.get("#")
                    cancel = params.__class__ is dict and params.get("cancel") is True
                    good = []
                    for path, _val in leaves_of(entry, []):
                        dotted = ".".join(path)
                        spec = LEAVES.get(dotted)
                        if spec is None or not spec[4]:
                            fail(["osc", "state", "subscribe"] + path, 404)
                            continue
                        if not cancel and not holds(spec[3]):
                            fail(path, 406)
                            continue
                        good.append(path)
                        if cancel:
                            subs = [p for p in subs if p != dotted]
                        else:
                            if dotted not in subs:
                                subs.append(dotted)
                            initial.append((path, current(spec)))
                    if not good:
                        continue
                    # The echo of an entry, one member per address.
                    parts = []
                    if params.__class__ is dict:
                        parts.append(dumps({"#": params})[1:-1])
                    for path in good:
                        parts.append(dumps(tree(path, None))[1:-1])
                    echoed.append("{" + ",".join(parts) + "}")
                state["_subscriptions"] = ",".join(subs)
                if echoed:
                    members.append('"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[' + ",".join(echoed) + "]}}")
                for path, val in initial:
                    member(path, val)

            def handle(path, value):
                dotted = ".".join(path)
                if dotted == "osc.xid":
                    member(path, value)
                elif dotted == "osc.state.subscribe":
                    subscribe(value)
                elif dotted == "osc.state.close":
                    state["_subscriptions"] = ""
                    member(path, True)
                elif dotted in OSC:
                    if value is not None:
                        fail(path, 406)
                    else:
                        member(path, OSC[dotted])
                elif dotted in LEAVES:
                    spec = LEAVES[dotted]
                    if not holds(spec[3]):
                        fail(path, 406)
                    elif value is None:
                        if spec[0] in ("trigger", "confirm", "power_down"):
                            fail(path, 406)
                        else:
                            member(path, current(spec))
                    else:
                        result, code = apply(spec, value)
                        if result is NO:
                            fail(path, code)
                        else:
                            member(path, result)
                else:
                    fail(path, 404)

            try:
                request = json.loads(text)
                if request.__class__ is not dict:
                    raise ValueError("not an object")
            except ValueError:
                respond('{"osc":{"error":[400]}}')
                return

            for path, value in leaves_of(request, []):
                handle(path, value)
            if errors:
                members.append(dumps({"osc": {"error": errors}})[1:-1])
            respond("{" + ",".join(members) + "}")

        _run()
